WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Since you are tired and I have a sore throat, I will be very brief.

00:06.000 --> 00:15.000
The place where we are now was my family's cow stable.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.000
Will you two translate? Very good.

00:22.000 --> 00:27.000
(Translation) You are tired, he has a sore throat, so it will be quick.

00:27.000 --> 00:35.000
(Translation) The place where you are now is where the cows lived in his family's time.

00:35.000 --> 00:41.000
Old man, kaput.

00:41.000 --> 00:48.000
Many Germans understand that very well. Kaput, you know?

00:49.000 --> 00:55.000
I was born 89 years ago in the house above, in this house.

00:55.000 --> 01:07.000
So, naturally, my throat has grown old too.

01:07.000 --> 01:20.000
But old as it is, I have the duty to explain to you a little of what is here.

01:20.000 --> 01:29.000
(Translation) It is old, but he really wants to explain to you what is in here.

01:29.000 --> 01:35.000
This was my family's cow stable.

01:35.000 --> 01:44.000
(Translation) This is where the cows lived in his parents' and grandfather's days.

01:44.000 --> 01:53.000
And now, if I ask you what this is, I know what you will say: the dining room.

01:53.000 --> 02:02.000
(Translation) If he asks you what this is, he knows you will say: this is where we eat.

02:02.000 --> 02:12.000
Dining room.

02:12.000 --> 02:17.000
We eat here, but it is not the dining room.

02:17.000 --> 02:22.000
This is a museum.

02:22.000 --> 02:41.000
It comes from the Journey to the University of Life, in this vehicle, this Land Rover,

02:41.000 --> 02:46.000
through Africa and Latin America,

02:46.000 --> 02:52.000
to get to know the popular cultures that are not taught at university.

02:52.000 --> 03:09.000
When the journey ended, the museum you see here was created with this vehicle.

03:09.000 --> 03:28.000
But in our society we care little for the spirit and a lot for the body: we come in tired and hungry, and all we see are tables and food.

03:28.000 --> 03:39.000
That is why, when I ask what this is: not a dining room. It is a museum.

03:39.000 --> 03:54.000
(Translation) We are tired and just want to eat, so we do not open our eyes and see that we are in a museum, not a dining room.

03:54.000 --> 04:23.000
To finish: whoever wants can come to the small hermitage at the end of the albergue. Inside are important paintings of the way of life, which goes from manipulation to liberation.

04:23.000 --> 04:37.000
(Translation) He will be in the hermitage to explain the paintings of the way of life, from slavery to liberation.

04:37.000 --> 04:46.000
In ten minutes I will be there to explain this way.

04:46.000 --> 04:59.000
In my opinion, it is the most important place on the whole Camino del Norte.

04:59.000 --> 05:17.000
It is no monument, but a small space with a great idea spread across the whole world: the way of life, from manipulation and slavery to liberation.

05:17.000 --> 05:29.000
(Translation) It is not a big building, but for him the idea behind these paintings is essential. So he invites you to go.
